Problem:


errors--> automatic recovery --> retried task --> duplicates

idempotency : how many times you run a processing job, you always get the same result , without duplicates

Solution


Overwriting
-------------
-remove data before writing data 

Pattern 1:
Fast Metadata Cleaner
 DROP TABLE + TRUNCATE TABLE; better than delete as delete involves 2 steps. 

when reaches the executionday, truncate or delete data, if not just insert data normally

Gotchas:
1) Have to backfill the whole week if one day is affected.
2) Metadata limits --> can add a freezing step like making the data monthly /yearly after confirming no further changes
3) Data not in single point anymore, need to group it those and expose as a single unit.
4) Schema evolution- add new field.


Pattern 2:
Data Overwrite
-sometimes metadata is not possible,
-set a setting to clean the file before writing
For example: SQL : DELETE FROM & INSERT INTO/ INSERT & OVERWRITE

Gotchas:
1) data overhead
- data not partitioned might be too big to handle. --> should do some partitioning.
2) might need a vacuum to 

